
EXPERIMENT NO. 6

TITLE: To Deploy and Manage Containers Using Kubernetes.

STEP 1: Verify Kubernetes Installation

Open CMD and execute:

kubectl version --client

kubectl get nodes

Expected result: The node docker-desktop should show STATUS as Ready.


STEP 2: Create a Kubernetes Deployment

Run:

kubectl create deployment asdd-app --image=nginx

Expected output:
deployment.apps/asdd-app created


STEP 3: Check the Deployment

Run:

kubectl get deployments

Wait until READY shows 1/1.


STEP 4: Check the Pods

Run:

kubectl get pods

Wait until the pod status becomes Running.


STEP 5: Expose the Deployment

Run:

kubectl expose deployment asdd-app --type=NodePort --port=80

Expected output:
service/asdd-app exposed


STEP 6: Check the Service

Run:

kubectl get services

Verify that the asdd-app service has been created.


STEP 7: Access the Application

Run:

kubectl port-forward service/asdd-app 8080:80

Keep this CMD window open.

Open the browser and visit:

http://localhost:8080

Expected result: The Nginx Welcome page should appear.

Press Ctrl + C in CMD when you want to stop port forwarding.


STEP 8: Scale the Deployment

Run:

kubectl scale deployment asdd-app --replicas=3

Expected output:
deployment.apps/asdd-app scaled


STEP 9: Verify the Replicas 

Run:

kubectl get deployments

kubectl get pods

Expected result: Three pods should be running once they are ready.


STEP 10: Update the Application Image

Run:

kubectl set image deployment/asdd-app nginx=nginx:1.27

Note: If the image tag is unavailable or causes an error, use a valid Nginx image tag.

Check the update:

kubectl rollout status deployment/asdd-app

Expected result:
deployment "asdd-app" successfully rolled out


STEP 11: Verify All Resources in 2nd cmd

Run:

kubectl get deployments

kubectl get pods

kubectl get services

Confirm that the deployment has three replicas and the pods are running.


STEP 12: Clean Up the Resources

After completing the practical demonstration, run:

kubectl delete service asdd-app

kubectl delete deployment asdd-app

Expected output:
service "asdd-app" deleted
deployment.apps "asdd-app" deleted


RESULT:

Successfully deployed and managed an Nginx application using Kubernetes. Created a deployment, exposed it through a service, accessed the application, scaled replicas, updated the container image, and verified the Kubernetes resources.
